 ## Overview
-Vector normalization converts a 3D vector into a unit vector (magnitude 1) or identifies its dominant axis, serving as a fundamental preprocessing step for vector field visualization, compression, and geometric calculations in volume rendering. It differs from [Octahedral Normal Encoding](5029-octahedral-normal-encoding.md) by producing a full 3D float vector rather than a compressed 2D coordinate, and from [Half-Precision Float Conversion](3267-half-precision-float-conversion.md) by focusing on directional magnitude rather than bit-depth reduction.
+Vector normalization converts a 3D vector to unit length or identifies its dominant axis, serving as a fundamental preprocessing step for vector field visualization, compression, and geometric calculations in volume rendering [S1][S3, unofficial][S5][S6, unofficial]. The method encompasses standard Euclidean normalization (unitizing), maximum-index identification, and L-infinity normalization for specific eigenvector storage contexts [S1][S2, S3, S6, unofficial].
 
