 ### [Octahedral Normal Decoding](3373-octahedral-normal-decoding.md)
-Decodes a 2D octahedral coordinate into a 3D unit vector. It serves as the inverse operation for octahedral normal encoding, reconstructing surface normals from compressed 2D representations. It differs from [Octahedral Normal Encoding](5029-octahedral-normal-encoding.md) by performing the inverse mapping (index to vector) rather than the forward mapping, and from [Data-Dependent Normal Vector Quantizer (Simulated Annealing)](5865-data-dependent-normal-vector-quantizer-simulated-annealing.md) by using a fixed geometric distribution rather than a data-driven one.
